==English==

===Etymology===
Via {{etyl|fr}} {{term|pastiche|lang=fr}}, from {{etyl|it}} {{term|pasticcio||pie, something blended|lang=it}}, from {{VL.|en}} *{{term||pasticium}}, from {{etyl|la|en}} {{term|pasta||dough, pastry cake, paste|lang=la}}, from {{etyl|grc|en}} {{term|παστά||barley porridge|tr=pasta|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}, from {{term|παστός||sprinkled with salt|tr=pastos|lang=grc|sc=polytonic}}.

===Pronunciation===
* {{rhymes|iːʃ}}

===Noun===
{{en-noun}}

# A [[work]] of [[drama]], [[literature]], [[music]], or [[architecture]] that [[imitate]]s the work of a [[previous]] [[artist]], often [[satirically]].
# A [[musical]] [[medley]].
# An [[incongruous]] [[mixture]]; a [[hodgepodge]].
# A [[postmodern]] [[playwriting]] technique that fuses a variety of styles, genres, and story lines to create a new form.

